    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`check_quantized_moe_compatibility` requires, for block-quantized MoE checkpoints, that each rank's expert intermediate shard (`moe_intermediate_size / moe_tp_size`) is a multiple of the checkpoint's `weight_block_size[0]`. That is the right default for models that load the FP8 blocks as-is, but some model implementations do not depend on checkpoint block boundaries.\n\nConcrete case: GLM-5.2-FP8 served at TP64 by an out-of-tree platform plugin (AWS Neuron). Per rank, `moe_intermediate_size` is 2048 / 64 = 32, below the 128 block, so the check rejects the config. That plugin's model dequantizes the checkpoint blocks with each shard's offsets during loading and requantizes the experts per row, so partial-block shards are fine. Today the plugin has to monkeypatch `check_quantized_moe_compatibility` to get past this.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `model_loader/utils.py`: add `supports_quantized_moe_partial_block_shards(model_config)`, which resolves the model class via `get_model_architecture` (so OOT registry overrides are honored) and reads a `supports_quantized_moe_partial_block_shards` class attribute (default `False`). Same pattern as the existing `supports_cuda_vmm_feature_transport`.\n- `moe_ep_setup.check_quantized_moe_compatibility`: skip only the block-alignment error when the model class opts in. The `moe_intermediate_size % moe_tp_size` divisibility check is unchanged. The class is resolved only when the alignment check would otherwise fail, so passing configs and models that don't opt in behave exactly as before.\n- New CPU unit test `test/registered/unit/model_executor/model_runner_components/test_moe_ep_setup.py`:\n  - misaligned shards (2048 at TP64, 128 block) still raise for a model without the attribute\n  - the same config passes when the registered class opts in\n  - the divisibility check still applies to opted-in models\n  - aligned configs pass without resolving the model class\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A. No model forward or kernel changes; existing models keep the current behavior.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39913929922](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39913929922)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39913929760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39913929760)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39913929816](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39913929816)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
